## psc/sema/symbols/scope.pengu — scopes léxicos.
##
## Cada scope guarda un mapa `NameId -> SymbolId`. Usar `NameId` como clave
## evita copiar strings y hace que el lookup sea un entero. Los scopes se
## apilan en `SemaSymbols`; este módulo solo conoce la estructura y las
## operaciones puras de un scope.
##
## ## Memoria
## Cada `SemaScope` posee sus dos mapas. `SemaSymbols.free` los libera.

insignia sema_scope_

## Clase de scope.
omen SemaScopeKind:
    ## Scope global del programa.
    SgGlobal
    ## Cuerpo de una función.
    SgWeave
    ## Cuerpo de `enchanting`.
    SgEnchanting
    ## Cuerpo de una lambda.
    SgLambda
    ## Bloque de `if`/`unless`.
    SgIf
    ## Bloque de `while`.
    SgWhile
    ## Bloque de `for`.
    SgFor
    ## Bloque `with target:`.
    SgWith
    ## Bloque `or:`.
    SgOrBlock
    ## Bloque genérico.
    SgBlock
    ## Bloque `test`.
    SgTest

## Scope léxico.
##
## ## Memoria
## Sin destructor; `free_scope` libera los mapas.
rune SemaScope:
    ## Índice del scope padre (`-1` en global).
    parent as int
    ## Clase.
    kind as SemaScopeKind
    ## `NameId -> SymbolId`.
    bindings as map of int to int
    ## Tipo del target de `with` (`-1` si no).
    with_type as int
    ## `with` acepta `set`/métodos mutables.
    with_mutable as bool
    ## `NameId` del nombre del target de `with`.
    with_target as int
    ## Tipo de `enchanting` (`-1` si no).
    enchanting_type as int
    ## Tipo de retorno de la función (`-1` si no).
    return_type as int
    ## `true` dentro de un loop.
    in_loop as bool
    ## `true` dentro de `or:`.
    in_or_block as bool
    ## `true` dentro de un método ritual.
    is_ritual as bool
    ## Primera línea del scope.
    start_line as int
    ## Última línea del scope.
    end_line as int
    ## `NameId` del label del loop (`-1` si no).
    loop_label as int
    ## Labels de loops anidados visibles: `NameId -> label id`.
    loop_labels as map of int to int
    ## Primer bound de concepto visible (`types.bounds`).
    bounds_first as int
    ## Número de bounds visibles.
    bounds_count as int

## Crea un scope.
##
## ## Memoria
## Asigna dos mapas; liberar con `free_scope`.
weave new_scope with kind as SemaScopeKind, parent as int, start_line as int, end_line as int into SemaScope:
    return with parent is parent, kind is kind, bindings is map of int to int, with_type is -1, with_mutable is false, with_target is -1, enchanting_type is -1, return_type is -1, in_loop is false, in_or_block is false, is_ritual is false, start_line is start_line, end_line is end_line, loop_label is -1, loop_labels is map of int to int, bounds_first is 0, bounds_count is 0

## Libera los mapas del scope.
##
## ## Memoria
## Libera `bindings` y `loop_labels`.
weave free_scope with s as ref to SemaScope into void:
    banish s->bindings
    banish s->loop_labels

## Define un símbolo en el scope.
##
## Si el nombre ya existe, el último gana (stage0 hace lo mismo en locales).
##
## ## Memoria
## O(1) promedio; el mapa copia la cabecera del int.
weave scope_define with s as ref to SemaScope, name as int, symbol as int into void:
    calling s->bindings.put with name, symbol

## Lookup local.
##
## ## Memoria
## O(1) promedio; no asigna.
weave scope_lookup_local with s as ref to SemaScope, name as int into int:
    if calling s->bindings.has with name:
        return calling s->bindings.get with name
    return -1

## ¿Existe el nombre en este scope?
##
## ## Memoria
## O(1) promedio.
weave has_local with s as ref to SemaScope, name as int into bool:
    return calling s->bindings.has with name

## Número de nombres locales.
##
## ## Memoria
## O(1).
weave local_count with s as ref to SemaScope into int:
    return s->bindings.len

## Define un label de loop.
##
## ## Memoria
## O(1) promedio.
weave define_label with s as ref to SemaScope, name as int, label_id as int into void:
    calling s->loop_labels.put with name, label_id

## Lookup de label local.
##
## ## Memoria
## O(1) promedio.
weave lookup_label with s as ref to SemaScope, name as int into int:
    if calling s->loop_labels.has with name:
        return calling s->loop_labels.get with name
    return -1
